{
  "_doc": "How each architecture resolves a manifest's preprocessing: registry.Manifest.PreprocessSpec, then the model package's Arch.Resolve with its own adjustments (SCRFD's legacy normalize in 0..255 units, CLIP's default size and mean/std), or FixedByExport for architectures whose export fixes the preprocessing. Run by internal/vision/preprocess/arch_sync_test.go (models.New + ResolvedPreprocess) and clients/python/tests/test_go_python_sync.py (convert.spec.resolve_arch). `spec` is the resolved spec (absent fields: zero / empty, rescale defaults to true); `error` lists substrings the error must contain; `fixed_by_export: true` means the model loads and its input.* fields are reference only.",
